# Frontend settings. Copy to `.env` and fill in before building.
#
# Vite reads this at BUILD TIME and writes the value into the generated
# JavaScript. Editing it after `npm run build` changes nothing — the frontend
# must be rebuilt for a new value to take effect.

# Where the backend API lives.
#
# LEAVE EMPTY when the dashboard and the API share one domain. Every request
# then goes to `/api/...` on whatever domain the page was opened from, and the
# web server forwards it to the backend:
#
#     location /api/ { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:4000; }
#
# This is the setup the current production build uses, and it needs no CORS
# configuration because the browser sees a single domain.
#
# SET IT to the backend's full address only when the API is on a DIFFERENT
# domain or port, e.g.
#
#     VITE_API_BASE=https://api.yourdomain.com
#
# In that case the backend's CORS_ORIGIN must also list the dashboard's domain,
# and both sides must be https — a https page cannot call a http API.
#
# Not needed for local development: vite.config.ts already proxies /api to
# http://localhost:4000.
VITE_API_BASE=
